# Build context for web/Dockerfile, which is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT:
#
#   docker build -f web/Dockerfile -t polyemesis-site .
#
# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the root
# .dockerignore, so this file governs the site image and the root one keeps
# governing the release images (it excludes docs/, which the site needs).
#
# An ALLOW-LIST: everything is excluded, then only what web/Dockerfile COPYs is
# let back in. Keep the two in step -- a path added to a COPY line has to be
# re-included here or the build fails with "not found".
*

!web/
!docs/
!deploy/
!internal/
!integrations/
!scripts/
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!SECURITY.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!LICENSE
!config.example.yaml
!docker-compose.yml

# Then out again, inside the allowed directories: dependencies and build output
# (the image installs and builds its own), test fixtures, and anything
# secret-shaped, so a local file can never ride into a build layer.
**/node_modules
**/.git
web/dist
web/.astro
internal/web/dist
integrations/**/bin
**/testdata
**/*.db
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/id_rsa*
